id: SECRETS-066
title: HashiCorp Vault Token
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
patterns:
  - regex: hvs\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{24,}
    message: HashiCorp Vault service token detected. This grants access to secrets stored in Vault, potentially compromising all managed credentials.
fix: Revoke the token with `vault token revoke`. Use short-lived tokens with minimal policies and enable AppRole or Kubernetes auth for applications.
